+#### I-072 • A resting table cell acts where a right-click lands while a live editor acts on the word the platform seats under it, and the resting menu offers Speech and Share for a selection it doesn't hold.
+
+| Concern | Scale | Origin | Base | Date |
+|---------|-------|--------|------|------|
+| Low | Small (TBD) | Parallel Build | `cd813afdd` | **Created:** 11-03-2026<br>**Updated:** 11-03-2026 |
+
+**Description**
+
+A right-click on a page's or a focused cell's text lets the platform seat the word under it before the menu's reply, so every row but the list types acts on that word, while a resting cell defaults the press away and acts at the point the click lands. The two surfaces answer one gesture with two rules, so a Format ▸ row from an unselected word acts on that word in a live editor and at the click's point in a resting cell. The resting cell's general menu also carries Speech ▸ and Share ▸ beside a disabled Cut and Copy, because Chromium reports a `selectionText` the cell's own range doesn't hold, and Desktop builds those rows from Chromium's report rather than the request's.[^72]
+
+**Solution** [TBD]
+
+One rule for where a right-click acts, read by both surfaces from the request, and Desktop building Speech and Share from the same selection the request carries; which rule wins is a product call.
+
+#### I-073 • MarkdownPM's live coverage is split across five drives, so one editor change is driven five times over five launches.
+
+| Concern | Scale | Origin | Base | Date |
+|---------|-------|--------|------|------|
+| Minimal | Medium (TBD) | Parallel Build | `cd813afdd` | **Created:** 11-03-2026<br>**Updated:** 11-03-2026 |
+
+**Description**
+
+The editor's behavior is driven live by the List Types Drive, the Text Property Drive's TextPane group, the Path Links Drive's marks group, the Alias Drive's body picker group, and Editor Parity. Each launches its own instance on its own debug port over its own copy or backup of `~/Test` and seeds its own pages, so the five run one at a time, about ten minutes for one change, and an editor case lands in whichever drive its feature built rather than in one place a reader would look for it. Editor Parity also keeps its own launcher, CDP client, and fixtures beside `drive-harness.mjs`.[^73]
+
+**Solution** [TBD]
+
+One MarkdownPM drive on `drive-harness.mjs`, its groups holding the editor cases the five run today and Editor Parity's record-and-compare as one of its modes, so an editor change runs one launch; which cases move and which stay with their feature's drive is decided when it's built.
